{"text": "RT Reynolir- FILE COPY\n\nDAVID B. FISHEL\n\u2018Senior Vice President\nPublic Relations\n\nWinston-Salem, N.C. 27102\n919-741-7654 :\nSeptember 20, 1993\n\nMr. Owen Gay\nAssistant Producer\n\nWatchdog\nBritish Broadcasting Corp.\nWhite city\n201 Wood Lane\nLondon, England Wi2 77S\n\nDear Mr. Gay:\n\nTwo of the questions you posed to R.J. Reynolds Tobacco\nInternational were forwarded to me for response on behalf R.J.\nReynolds Tobacco Co., since Winston cigarettes are not sold in\nthe United Kingdom's domestic market, and the Joe Camel campaign\ndoes not appear in market there, either.\n\nI understand that you have interviewed David Goerlitz, a former\nmodel in one of our Winston campaigns. Not knowing specifically\nwhat Mr. Goerlitz has said to you, I will respond to the typical\nallegations he makes whenever interviewed.\n\nMr. Goerlitz was one of several models for Winston cigarettes\nduring the 1980s. Neither Mr. Goerlitz nor any other model was\never the \"Winston Man.\" Nor was Mr. Goerlitz ever retained in a\nmarketing consulting capacity for our company, so he never had\naccess to either our marketing strategies or executives.\nTherefore, any statements he might have made regarding the\ncompany's marketing practices should be considered as speculation\non his part, not based on any special knowledge of our industry.\n\nHis lack of knowledge of the brand's marketing efforts is\npatently evident if you simply check his statements that market\nshare increased during the time he was a model. Mr. Goerlitz has\nrepeatedly claimed to have moved the brand from 4th to 2nd place\nin U.S. cigarette sales, when in fact, during the time his photos\nappeared in our ads, Winston's market\u2019 share declined steadily.\nThe brand is currently the second-largest selling cigarette in\nAmerica, and has been since the 1970s -- well before his\nappearances in our ads.\n\n99TS zpTTS\n\n\u201cWe work for smokers.\u201d", "words": [{"text": "RT", "x0": 88, "y0": 60, "x1"